## 10. Time and Space Complexity of KNN

Let:
- \(n\) = Number of training records.
- \(d\) = Number of features.
- \(k\) = Number of nearest neighbors.

| Operation | Time Complexity |
|---|---|
| Training (storing data) | Approximately O(1) model-building work |
| Predicting one record | O(nd) for distance calculations, plus neighbor selection |
| Predicting multiple records | Depends on the number of test records |

KNN is called a **lazy learning algorithm** because it does very little work during training. Most of the computation happens when making predictions.

Its storage requirement is approximately O(nd), because it stores the training data.

